IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`

-- Israel: chapter 3 of the Interpretation Law 5741-1981, "the interpretation of powers": ss 11 to 19.
--
-- Each section says what a grant of power (or imposition of duty) in another enactment includes without saying so.
-- A rule here is a function over a small typed representation of the grant and of the thing done under it, and
-- answers whether the Law reads the grant as covering that thing. FALSE always means "this section does not extend
-- the grant to that thing", never "the thing is forbidden". Judgements the Law leaves open ("the proper speed",
-- "to a reasonable extent", "needed") are plain inputs. Every rule is subject to s 1's gate (il-interpretation-gate.l4):
-- where the Law is displaced the rule REFUSES.
--
-- For the individual: a grant of power read this way fixes what an authority may do to a person, and a duty read
-- this way fixes what a person is owed (s 11: the thing done with the proper speed; s 13(b): who is bound at a time).
-- Source: the unofficial Wikisource consolidation, ../../source/law.wiki (src:N). English glosses are mine; the Hebrew governs.

§ `Interpretation Law: the interpretation of powers (ss 11 to 19)`

§§ `Nouns`

-- s 11
DECLARE `Kind of authority to act` IS ONE OF
    `an authorisation`
    `an obligation`

DECLARE `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` HAS
    `its kind`                                      IS A `Kind of authority to act`
    `the enactment fixes a time for doing it`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What an authority to act with no time fixed amounts to` IS ONE OF
    `a power to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`
    `a duty to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`

-- s 12
DECLARE `What a power to give relief grants` IS ONE OF
    `an exemption`
    `a relief`
    `a discount`
    `something like an exemption, relief or discount`
    `something else`

DECLARE `The extent of what is granted` IS ONE OF
    `in full`
    `in part`

DECLARE `The terms of what is granted` IS ONE OF
    `without conditions`
    `on conditions`

-- s 13
DECLARE `What is done to a person under a power` IS ONE OF
    `appointing the person`
    `authorising the person`
    `imposing a duty on the person`

DECLARE `The way the person is designated` IS ONE OF
    `by naming the person`
    `by naming the person's office`
    `in some other way`

DECLARE `A holder of an office` HAS
    `person`  IS A STRING
    `from`    IS A DATE
    `until`   IS A DATE

-- What a designation names (s 13(b) speaks of the office alone; the other two are the gap it leaves).
DECLARE `What a designation names` IS ONE OF
    `the person by name alone` HAS `the person named` IS A STRING
    `the office by name alone`
    `the person by name and the office by name`

-- s 14
DECLARE `Something done about an appointment` IS ONE OF
    `making the appointment`
    `suspending its validity`
    `cancelling it`
    `dismissing the appointee`
    `suspending the appointee from the post`
    `something else`

-- s 15
DECLARE `What a power to make rules concerns` IS ONE OF
    `regulations`
    `an administrative direction`
    `something else`

DECLARE `What is done to the regulations or direction` IS ONE OF
    `amending them`
    `changing them`
    `suspending them`
    `cancelling them`
    `something else`

DECLARE `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` HAS
    `what they are`                                  IS A `What a power to make rules concerns`
    `what is done to them`                           IS A `What is done to the regulations or direction`
    `it is done in the way they were made or given`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 16
DECLARE `An appointment connected with a body of members` IS ONE OF
    `a chairman for the body`
    `an alternate for a member`
    `an alternate for the chairman`
    `something else`

-- s 17
DECLARE `What an authority is for` IS ONE OF
    `to do a thing`
    `to hear a matter`
    `to decide a matter`
    `to compel the doing of a thing`
    `something else`

-- s 18
DECLARE `What is done on an appeal or objection` IS ONE OF
    `confirming the decision without changes`
    `confirming the decision with changes`
    `cancelling the decision`
    `deciding another decision in its place`
    `returning the matter with instructions to the authority that decided`
    `returning the matter without instructions`
    `something else`

§§ `Named refusals`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 19 speaks only of the grant by itself; whether something else in an enactment takes away the other power or duty is for that enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 19 speaks only of the grant by itself; whether something else in an enactment takes away the other power or duty is for that enactment"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 13(b) speaks of a designation by the name of the office alone; a designation by the person's name and the office's name is outside it` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 13(b) speaks of a designation by the name of the office alone; a designation by the person's name and the office's name is outside it, and neither it nor s 13(a) says whether such a designation binds the person named or whoever fills the office"

§§ `s 11 — no time fixed`

-- src:90 | הסמכה או חיוב לעשות דבר, בלי קביעת זמן לעשייתו – משמעם שיש סמכות או חובה לעשותו במהירות הראויה ולחזור ולעשותו מזמן לזמן ככל הנדרש לפי הנסיבות.
@ref Interpretation Law s 11 (src:90)
GIVEN authority IS AN `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A `What an authority to act with no time fixed amounts to`
`s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` authority `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   authority's `the enactment fixes a time for doing it`
         THEN `s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed`
         ELSE CONSIDER authority's `its kind`
              WHEN `an authorisation` THEN `a power to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`
              WHEN `an obligation`    THEN `a duty to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`)

-- "With the proper speed" is open-textured and fixes no number of days; whether the time taken was the proper speed
-- is a judgement of the case, and so a plain input. The Law gives no deadline, and none is invented.
@ref Interpretation Law s 11 (src:90)
GIVEN authority IS AN `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing`
      `the time taken was the proper speed in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11 — the thing was done in time:` authority `, the time taken being the proper speed:` `the time taken was the proper speed in the circumstances` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   authority's `the enactment fixes a time for doing it`
         THEN `s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed`
         ELSE `the time taken was the proper speed in the circumstances`)

-- "Again from time to time as the circumstances require": whether the circumstances require it is a judgement input.
@ref Interpretation Law s 11 (src:90)
GIVEN authority IS AN `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing`
      `the circumstances require it to be done again` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11 — it is to be done again:` authority `, the circumstances requiring it:` `the circumstances require it to be done again` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   authority's `the enactment fixes a time for doing it`
         THEN `s 11 speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed`
         ELSE `the circumstances require it to be done again`)

§§ `s 12 — a power to give relief`

-- src:93 | הסמכה ליתן פטור, הקלה, הנחה וכיוצא באלה – משמעה הסמכה ליתן אותם אף במקצת או בתנאים.
@ref Interpretation Law s 12 (src:93)
GIVEN granted IS A `What a power to give relief grants`
      extent IS A `The extent of what is granted`
      terms IS A `The terms of what is granted`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12 — a power to grant exemption, relief or a discount covers granting` granted extent terms `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER granted
         WHEN `an exemption`                                  THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a relief`                                      THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a discount`                                    THEN TRUE
         WHEN `something like an exemption, relief or discount` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `something else`                                THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 13 — appointment and authorisation: how`

-- src:96 | (א) מקום שניתנה סמכות למנות אדם, להסמיכו או להטיל עליו חובה – מותר לעשות כן בנקיבת שמו או בנקיבת שם משרתו.
@ref Interpretation Law s 13(a) (src:96)
GIVEN done IS A `What is done to a person under a power`
      way IS A `The way the person is designated`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(a) — the power to appoint, authorise or charge a person may be exercised` done way `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER way
         WHEN `by naming the person`          THEN TRUE
         WHEN `by naming the person's office` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `in some other way`             THEN FALSE)

-- The person bound at a time by a designation that names the office alone is whoever fills the office at that time.
-- The holder's last day is "until" (Law s 8), so it is included. NOTHING when the office had no holder that day:
-- the text names no one in that case, and none is supplied. The holders are a list the caller has from the register
-- of the office; the text does not say what to do if two holders' terms overlap, and the first listed is taken.
-- src:97 | (ב) מינוי אדם, הסמכתו או הטלת חובה עליו בנקיבת שם משרתו בלבד – משמעם מינוי, הסמכה או חיוב של מי שממלא את המשרה מזמן לזמן.
@ref Interpretation Law s 13(b) (src:97)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 13(b) — the person bound on` day `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` holders `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (foldr pick NOTHING holders
         WHERE
             pick h rest MEANS
                 IF   h's `from` AT MOST day AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (h's `until`)
                 THEN JUST (h's `person`)
                 ELSE rest)

-- What the designation names. Name alone: the person named is bound (s 13(a) lets the designation name the person, and (b)
-- is about the office alone). Office alone: s 13(b) above. Name AND office: (b) does not speak of it, so the module refuses.
@ref Interpretation Law s 13(b) (what the designation names) (src:97)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      names IS A `What a designation names`
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 13(b) — the person bound on` day `by a designation that names` names `, among the holders` holders `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER names
         WHEN `the person by name alone` person                  THEN JUST person
         WHEN `the office by name alone`                         THEN `s 13(b) — the person bound on` day `by a designation naming the office alone, among the holders` holders `, for` matter
         WHEN `the person by name and the office by name`        THEN `s 13(b) speaks of a designation by the name of the office alone; a designation by the person's name and the office's name is outside it`)

-- Whether the rule of (b) (whoever fills the office from time to time) applies to the designation: only to a designation that names the
-- office alone. A designation by the person's name alone binds the person named and does not pass to the next holder; one by name and
-- office together is outside (b)'s words.
@ref Interpretation Law s 13(b) (whether the rule applies) (src:97)
GIVEN names IS A `What a designation names`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(b) — the rule that the office-holder from time to time is bound applies to a designation that names` names `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER names
         WHEN `the person by name alone` person                  THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the office by name alone`                         THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the person by name and the office by name`        THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 14 — a power of appointment`

-- src:100 | הסמכה לעשות מינוי – משמעה גם הסמכה להתלות את תקפו, לבטלו, לפטר את מי שנתמנה או להשעותו מתפקידו.
@ref Interpretation Law s 14 (src:100)
GIVEN done IS A `Something done about an appointment`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14 — a power to make an appointment covers` done `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER done
         WHEN `making the appointment`                    THEN TRUE
         WHEN `suspending its validity`                   THEN TRUE
         WHEN `cancelling it`                             THEN TRUE
         WHEN `dismissing the appointee`                  THEN TRUE
         WHEN `suspending the appointee from the post`    THEN TRUE
         WHEN `something else`                            THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction`

-- src:103 | הסמכה להתקין תקנות או ליתן הוראת מינהל – משמעה גם הסמכה לתקנן, לשנותן, להתלותן או לבטלן בדרך שהותקנו התקנות או ניתנה ההוראה.
@ref Interpretation Law s 15 (src:103)
GIVEN step IS A `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15 — a power to make regulations or give a direction covers` step `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    (   step's `what they are` EQUALS `regulations`
              OR step's `what they are` EQUALS `an administrative direction`)
         AND (   step's `what is done to them` EQUALS `amending them`
              OR step's `what is done to them` EQUALS `changing them`
              OR step's `what is done to them` EQUALS `suspending them`
              OR step's `what is done to them` EQUALS `cancelling them`)
         AND step's `it is done in the way they were made or given`)

§§ `s 16 — a power to appoint a body of several members`

-- "Several" (מספר) is taken as at least two members (a fork, see NOTES.md); the Law does not say. An alternate "for each
-- member" reaches the chairman's alternate only if the chairman is one of the members.
-- src:106 | הסמכה למנות גוף של מספר חברים – משמעה גם הסמכה למנות לו יושב ראש ולמנות ממלא מקום לכל חבר שלו.
@ref Interpretation Law s 16 (src:106)
GIVEN members IS A NUMBER
      appointment IS AN `An appointment connected with a body of members`
      `the chairman is one of the members` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16 — a power to appoint a body of` members `members covers` appointment `, the chairman being a member:` `the chairman is one of the members` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    members AT LEAST 2
         AND CONSIDER appointment
             WHEN `a chairman for the body`        THEN TRUE
             WHEN `an alternate for a member`      THEN TRUE
             WHEN `an alternate for the chairman`  THEN `the chairman is one of the members`
             WHEN `something else`                 THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 17 — ancillary powers`

-- src:109 | (א) הסמכה לעשות דבר או לדון בענין פלוני או להכריע בו – משמעה גם הסמכה לקבוע נוהל עבודה וסדרי דיונים ככל שאלה לא נקבעו בחיקוק.
@ref Interpretation Law s 17(a) (src:109)
GIVEN for IS A `What an authority is for`
      `an enactment has fixed the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(a) — an authority` for `covers fixing its working procedure and order of proceedings, an enactment having fixed them:` `an enactment has fixed the procedure` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    (   for EQUALS `to do a thing`
              OR for EQUALS `to hear a matter`
              OR for EQUALS `to decide a matter`)
         AND NOT `an enactment has fixed the procedure`)

-- src:110 | (ב) הסמכה לעשות דבר או לכפות עשייתו – משמעה גם מתן סמכויות עזר הדרושות לכך במידה המתקבלת על הדעת.
@ref Interpretation Law s 17(b) (src:110)
GIVEN for IS A `What an authority is for`
      `the ancillary power is needed for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to a reasonable extent` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(b) — an authority` for `covers an ancillary power, needed:` `the ancillary power is needed for it` `, reasonable:` `to a reasonable extent` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    (   for EQUALS `to do a thing`
              OR for EQUALS `to compel the doing of a thing`)
         AND `the ancillary power is needed for it`
         AND `to a reasonable extent`)

§§ `s 18 — appeal and objection`

-- src:113 | הסמכה לדון ולהכריע בערר או בהשגה אחרת על החלטה של רשות – משמעה גם הסמכה לאשר את ההחלטה בשינויים או בלא שינוי, לבטלה ולהחליט החלטה אחרת במקומה או להחזיר את הענין עם הוראות לרשות שהחליטה.
@ref Interpretation Law s 18 (src:113)
GIVEN `the authority hears an appeal or objection against the decision of an authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      done IS A `What is done on an appeal or objection`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18 — the power to hear and decide an appeal or objection, if it hears one against an authority's decision:` `the authority hears an appeal or objection against the decision of an authority` `, covers` done `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    `the authority hears an appeal or objection against the decision of an authority`
         AND CONSIDER done
             WHEN `confirming the decision without changes`  THEN TRUE
             WHEN `confirming the decision with changes`     THEN TRUE
             WHEN `cancelling the decision`                  THEN TRUE
             WHEN `deciding another decision in its place`   THEN TRUE
             WHEN `returning the matter with instructions to the authority that decided` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `returning the matter without instructions` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `something else`                           THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 19 — powers and duties under other enactments are kept`

-- "In themselves" (כשהם לעצמם): the grant, by itself, takes nothing away. Something else in an enactment may; that is for
-- that enactment, and the rule REFUSES if the caller says there is such a thing.
-- src:116 | מתן סמכות או הטלת חובה לפי חיקוק אחד, אין בהם כשהם לעצמם כדי לגרוע מסמכות שניתנה או חובה שהוטלה לפי חיקוק אחר.
@ref Interpretation Law s 19 (src:116)
GIVEN `something other than the grant itself takes away the other power or duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19 — a grant of power or an imposition of duty, by itself, takes away from a power or duty under another enactment, something else doing so:` `something other than the grant itself takes away the other power or duty` `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   `something other than the grant itself takes away the other power or duty`
         THEN `s 19 speaks only of the grant by itself; whether something else in an enactment takes away the other power or duty is for that enactment`
         ELSE FALSE)

§§ `s 20 — an act imposed on several persons, where the enactment requires all of them to act`

-- Law s 20 gives way to "another provision on the matter" (s 1): an enactment that requires all the persons to act is one.
-- This calls pass 1's `s 20 — an act imposed on` ... through s 1's gate, with the requirement as the other provision.
-- src:119 | פעולה שהוטלה על מספר בני אדם כשרה אם נעשתה בידי רובם.
@ref Interpretation Law s 20 (src:119)
GIVEN requiresAll IS A BOOLEAN
      total IS A NUMBER
      acted IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20 — where the enactment's requirement that all act is` requiresAll `, an act imposed on` total `persons was validly done when` acted MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for`
        (IF requiresAll THEN `a matter another provision deals with` ELSE `a matter nothing displaces`)
        `is`
        (`s 20 — an act imposed on` total `persons was validly done when` acted `of them did it`)

@ref Interpretation Law s 20 (whether s 20 applies) (src:119)
GIVEN requiresAll IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20 — the rule of the majority applies to an act imposed on several persons, the enactment's requirement that all act being` requiresAll MEANS
    `s 1 — the Law governs` (IF requiresAll THEN `a matter another provision deals with` ELSE `a matter nothing displaces`)
